==========================================
DAY 10 NOTES — Disk & Storage Management
Date: 07-09-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- df -h = how full is the WHOLE filesystem (big picture)
- du -sh = how much space does THIS specific folder use (drill-down)
- lsblk = shows physical disks and partitions attached to the machine
- "Mounting" = attaching a storage device onto a folder in the filesystem tree
  (no drive letters like Windows — just becomes part of the one big tree)
- /dev/sda = first disk, /dev/sda1 = first partition on that disk
- ALWAYS umount a USB drive before physically removing it (avoids data corruption)
- df and du numbers don't always match exactly — they measure different things

COMMANDS I PRACTICED:
[ ] df -h
[ ] du -sh (folder-level usage)
[ ] lsblk / lsblk -f
[ ] mount / umount

fill this in after running commands yourself :
$ df -h
> 

$ du -sh ~
> 

$ lsblk
> 


